Tenaya, lawful male human Knight
Genoless, poly*less, artiwishless
26,399 turns


This was my first successful attempt at playing a "quick" game of
Nethack.  Basically, I've had less time to play lately so I wanted to
see how efficiently I could satisfy my fix of Nethack with a minimum
of real life time.  So, I opted for a knight given the fantastic
starting equipment and potent steed.  Playing polyless also sped
things up since if I am using polypiling I tend to packrat rings,
wands and armor.  Overall I did not feel like I played very fast, I
just didn't waste a bunch of time on extraneous things like magic trap
dancing, succubus dancing, excessive monster slaying, dungeon
exploring, poly trap dancing, etc.  I just got in and used wishes to
fill in gaps for my ascension kit.  An early pair of jumping boots
sped things up, too.

I finished the game in 26,400 turns, which is my personal best.  I
have stopped playing the Ascension Run, especially with pre-armored
classes, because it's just too much work and is not always even very
safe (thanks sjdevnull, KPD, and all you great folks on RGRN for some
good discussion).  Standard operating procedure for me now is to level
up my pet to XP 4 or 5 and then level up to XP 3 to keep safe from
attack wands and the odd trap.  I can spot a boulder trap when I see
one now so I disable those when found.  Anyhow I try to keep my pet
stronger than me and keep my XP to 4 or 5 until I reach Minetown,
which I do after completing Sokoban.

Overall, I play conservatively until I acquire Magic Resistance or
reflection. As I've found that a character running around with great
AC can lose that advantage upon finding a polymorph trap and turning
into something large, like a wumpus.  Following MR, my next task is to
acquire a luckstone, pray for holy water, bless the luckstone, find a
unicorn, and level up to XP=14 for the quest.  Then I go straight for
the castle with only slight detours for loot.  I'd say about half or
more of the levels in the game go unexplored this way but I still wind
up doing inventory management to keep from being burdened.

In this particular game I completed Sokoban (bag of holding) and at XP
5 (or so) I dipped for Excalibur and a wish (Grey Dragon Scale Mail,
please).  A co-aligned altar on level 4 gave me holy water and
Grayswandir.  I found two bones files that contributed to my loot and
one of them had a wand of wishing 1:0 (thanks Antiworld)!  Fortunately
I found 2 magic markers and that saved me a wish or two.  Weapons were
plentiful in this game as I found a silver saber Minetown (Xephania, I
exacted vengeance for you against the lizard and floating eye; thanks
for the loot!)  It looked like Xephania had bumped into a floating eye
in Minetown.  Speaking of which, I played much of the Ascension Run
without color because I couldn't see dark blue on my screen.  I also
found a cursed Frostbane in the Mines (I left it as I prefer
Grayswandir or even Excalibur).

My weapons options were: Frostbane, Excalibur, Silver Saber,
Grayswandir, Katana, and Lance.  I opted for Grayswandir #twoweaponed
with a katana.  Excalibur was carried until the Ascension Run, just in
case.  I kept the lance for jousting throughout the game.  I untrapped
every dart trap that I came across and used +0 darts when I needed a
missile weapon (e.g. krakens).  I never found a spellbook of magic
missile and by the end of the game I thought it wasteful to wish for
one, so I went without.

Throughout the game I used 6 of 8 wishes:
~ Grey Dragon Scale Mail - from fountain;
~ Blessed fixed gauntlets of dexterity - kind of a waste, should have
just kept with my +1  blessed leather gloves and enchanted them;
~ Blessed fixed greased helm of brilliance - kind of a waste, since I
did not do much spell casting but I wanted a better failure rate for
casting identify
~ 3 blessed scrolls of charging - too bad I had to wish for these
~ blessed brass lantern !!! I had no light source for my jumping boot
Ascension Run
~ and something else, maybe a magic marker.

The mid-game was relatively uneventful: I found a cockatrice corpse on
Medusa's level so I used that to clear the courtyard and one barracks
of the castle.  The second group of soldiers in the castle was left
sleeping.  Oh yeah, the quest was easy: I read a scroll of earth to
block the upstairs and beat Ixoth to death.

I used the Asmodeus Tour Guide and Courier Service for mapping my way
through Gehennom.  I level teleported with him down to the Vibrating
Square and let him show me the stairs going all the way up to
Baalzebub's level.  Orcus was relieved of his wand of death with a
potion of paralysis before he managed to use it.  Once I did the
invocation I let everyone's favorite Demon Prince bring me the Amulet
and then I kicked my steed into a gallop and jumped and teleported my
way through the plane of earth.  My faithful steed was left on the
plane of earth since he did not fly.

Rodney was killed 4 times each time with a wand of death, although he
did his best to dodge the rays.  Probably used 7 zaps total.
Pestilence was killed in melee without him having a turn to attack me
and I only had to visit 1 altar.  I only needed 3 or 4 teleport zaps
to jump my way to the altar.  Except for some insects, Pestilence was
the only casualty on the Astral Plane.  I should not neglect to
mention the benefit of a blessed Book of the Dead in taking care of
purple L's.  It's very handy.

Due to my haste, I lacked a conventional way to confuse myself on the
plane of fire.  My choices were to wish for a beer, wish for a crystal
ball, or possibly curse my unicorn horn and read my gold detection
that way.  Then I remembered (I slept on it) that a cursed scroll of
confuse monster might be able to do it, and thus use my magic markers
and a cursed blank scroll to confuse myself.  I did try to eat a
couple of cans of dog food, but to no avail.  Incidentally, I ate dog
food earlier in the game for fooproofing my jumping boots and katana.
I tend to be a bit hasty in diluting potions for holy water and then
later realize that I need to confuse myself.

Tenaya, lawful male human Knight






